","english":"chest"}],"notes":"Corpus backfill 2026-11-24; individually reviewed reusable expression. Authored lexical expression attested in learner corpus; requires semantic review."},"occurrence":{"canonicalId":"chapter:aee7e467-e411-424f-bc8f-bbb701c171ab","unitKey":"sentence/14","source":{"kind":"chapter","id":"aee7e467-e411-424f-bc8f-bbb701c171ab","title":"The Weight of Silence","parentId":"7826559a-871f-447c-90c1-a7b43b8b2a7f","parentTitle":"Half of The Water","language":"ar","url":"/admin/books/preview/aee7e467-e411-424f-bc8f-bbb701c171ab"},"arabic":"فِي الصَّبَاحِ الْبَاكِرِ رَأَتْهُ غَاضِبًا، ضَيِّقَ الصَّدْرِ بِأَسْئِلَتِهَا؛ وَالْآنَ عَادَ لَبِقًا، يُمَازِحُ الْقَادِمِينَ، وَيُحْسِنُ إِقْنَاعَهُمْ حَتَّى يَمُدُّوا أَيْدِيَهُمْ إِلَى نُقُودِهِمْ.","english":"Earlier that morning she had seen him angry, irritated by her questions; now he was charming again, joking with newcomers and skilfully persuading them until their hands reached for their purses.","timestamp":""}},{"fields":{"phrase_ar_di":"طَلَبُ العِلْمِ","phrase_tr":"ṭalab al-ʿilm","english":"seeking knowledge","cefr":"B1","word_glosses":[{"arabic":"طَلَبِ","english":"it was demanded / he was ordered"},{"arabic":"الْعِلْمِ","english":"the knowledge"}],"notes":"Corpus backfill 2026-11-24; individually reviewed reusable expression. Authored lexical expression attested in learner corpus; requires semantic review."},"occurrence":{"canonicalId":"chapter:350b338a-2289-44bc-a1f1-9fe5a7e7f550","unitKey":"sentence/66","source":{"kind":"chapter","id":"350b338a-2289-44bc-a1f1-9fe5a7e7f550","title":"Before the King","parentId":"e4ba3b2a-1a62-45ad-a2bb-1eff8a36fed7","parentTitle":"Lord of The Boy","language":"ar","url":"/admin/books/preview/350b338a-2289-44bc-a1f1-9fe5a7e7f550"},"arabic":"وَلَمْ يَكُنْ قَدْ مَضَى عَلَى إِيمَانِهِ مَا يُقَاسُ بِسِنِينَ الرَّاهِبِ فِي طَلَبِ الْعِلْمِ وَالْعِبَادَةِ.","english":"He had not been a believer for anything approaching the years the monk had spent seeking knowledge and worshipping God.","timestamp":""}},{"fields":{"phrase_ar_di":"عَجَزَ عَنْ","phrase_tr":"ʿajaza ʿan","english":"was unable to, failed to","cefr":"A2","word_glosses":[{"arabic":"عَجَزَ","english":"helplessness"},{"arabic":"عَنْ","english":"about / from"}],"notes":"Corpus backfill 2026-11-24; individually reviewed reusable expression. Authored lexical expression attested in learner corpus; requires semantic review."},"occurrence":{"canonicalId":"chapter:24238417-d5f5-48a6-9f0d-e3990e2490f2","unitKey":"sentence/134","source":{"kind":"chapter","id":"24238417-d5f5-48a6-9f0d-e3990e2490f2","title":"Half The Price of The Neighbor","parentId":"d203a5b6-c627-4b98-9166-a2f9ab46fefb","parentTitle":"The Opposite Door","language":"ar","url":"/admin/books/preview/24238417-d5f5-48a6-9f0d-e3990e2490f2"},"arabic":"لَمْ تَكُنْ تُرِيدُ أَنْ تَخْسَرَ جَارًا أَحْسَنَ إِلَيْهِمَا، وَلَا أَنْ تَخْسَرَ زَوْجَهَا بِسَبَبِ دَيْنٍ عَجَزَ عَنْ وَفَائِهِ.","english":"She did not want to lose a neighbour who had treated them kindly, nor did she want to lose her husband over a debt he could not pay.","timestamp":""}},{"fields":{"phrase_ar_di":"عَسَى أَنْ","phrase_tr":"ʿasā an","english":"may, hopefully","cefr":"B1","word_glosses":[{"arabic":"عَسَى","english":"perhaps / it may be"},{"arabic":"أَنْ","english":"that / to"}],"notes":"Corpus backfill 2026-11-24; individually reviewed reusable expression. Authored lexical expression attested in learner corpus; requires semantic review."},"occurrence":{"canonicalId":"chapter:8f661c70-bbbf-46ac-a563-a0f1f91fe5e5","unitKey":"sentence/13","source":{"kind":"chapter","id":"8f661c70-bbbf-46ac-a563-a0f1f91fe5e5","title":"Asiya in the Face of Falsehood","parentId":"f3b08eae-fdfc-4746-81b9-7b7d5088ff69","parentTitle":"The Fragrant Scent","language":"ar","url":"/admin/books/preview/8f661c70-bbbf-46ac-a563-a0f1f91fe5e5"},"arabic":"«قُرَّتُ عَيْنٍ لِي وَلَكَ لَا تَقْتُلُوهُ عَسَى أَنْ يَنْفَعَنَا أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا».","english":"‘A delight to my eyes and yours